    "safetyCenterTitle":  "Safety center",
    "safetyCenterIntro":  "A few simple rules to keep exchanges on ShelfShare pleasant and safe.",
    "safetyTip1Title":  "Meet during the day",
    "safetyTip1Desc":  "Schedule the exchange for a time with natural daylight, ideally morning or afternoon.",
    "safetyTip2Title":  "Choose a public place",
    "safetyTip2Desc":  "A café, bookstore, or mall is safer than someone\u0027s personal address.",
    "safetyTip3Title":  "Prefer locations with video surveillance",
    "safetyTip3Desc":  "Areas with security cameras discourage unpleasant behavior.",
    "safetyTip4Title":  "Don\u0027t share personal data",
    "safetyTip4Desc":  "You don\u0027t need to give your home address, ID number, or other sensitive data to make an exchange.",
    "safetyTip5Title":  "Check the rating and trust score",
    "safetyTip5Desc":  "A good history of completed exchanges is a good sign before meeting someone.",
    "safetyTip6Title":  "A real profile photo builds trust",
    "safetyTip6Desc":  "Profiles with a photo and a complete bio inspire more confidence in other users.",
    "safetyTip7Title":  "Check the book\u0027s condition before the exchange",
    "safetyTip7Desc":  "Compare the book to the listing\u0027s description before confirming the exchange as completed.",
    "safetyTip8Title":  "Report any suspicious behavior",
    "safetyTip8Desc":  "You can report or block a user directly from their profile or from the conversation.",
    "helpCenterTitle":  "FAQ",
    "helpFaq1Question":  "How does a book exchange work?",
    "helpFaq1Answer":  "You request a book from someone else\u0027s listing (you can also offer a book in exchange), the owner accepts or declines, then you arrange a meeting via chat. After you complete the exchange in person, either of you marks the exchange as completed.",
    "helpFaq2Question":  "What is the Trust Score?",
    "helpFaq2Answer":  "A 0-100 indicator calculated automatically from in-app activity: account age, verified email, how many exchanges you\u0027ve completed, your rating, how often you respond, and how rarely you cancel requests. It\u0027s not an identity check, just a behavior signal.",
    "helpFaq3Question":  "How is the \"bookstore\" price calculated?",
    "helpFaq3Answer":  "When you add a book with an ISBN, we try to find the list price on Google Books. Coverage is partial - not all books have a price available there, especially older or Romanian editions.",
    "helpFaq4Question":  "What does \"Fixed price, non-negotiable\" mean?",
    "helpFaq4Answer":  "If the seller checks this, buyers can no longer send price offers - the book can only be bought at the listed price.",
    "helpFaq5Question":  "How do I report or block a user?",
    "helpFaq5Answer":  "From the menu in the top-right corner of a conversation, or from a listing\u0027s detail page (the flag icon). Blocking stops messages in both directions.",
    "helpFaq6Question":  "What happens to the book after I sell it or give it in exchange?",
    "helpFaq6Answer":  "The listing becomes permanently unavailable. If the person who received it wants to list it again, they can do so from the Exchanges/Offers screen (\"Add to your library\") - the book\u0027s history stays traceable on its detail page, with photos from each owner.",
    "helpFaq7Question":  "Why doesn\u0027t a book show up in Categories or Similar Books?",
    "helpFaq7Answer":  "A book\u0027s genre comes from Open Library or Google Books when it\u0027s added - some books don\u0027t have a genre filled in on those external sources, especially less popular editions.",
    "helpCenterFooter":  "Didn\u0027t find your answer? You can report an issue directly from the conversation with the user involved.",
